# Services and EF Core

## Write results

Use `UserWriteResult` / `UserWriteStatus` (or the same pattern for new resources):

| Status | HTTP |
|---|---|
| Success | 201 create / 200 envelope for update-delete |
| NotFound | 404 |
| Forbidden | 403 (authz / system rules / bad caller) |
| ValidationFailed | 400 (blank fields, unknown RoleId, …) |
| Conflict | 409 (duplicate username/email) |

Include a clear `Message` when useful. Map in the controller via `ApiControllerBase` helpers — do not collapse validation into 403.

## Data rules

- Unique indexes on `Users.UserName`, `Users.Email`, `Roles.Name`, `Rights.Name`.
- Normalize username/email with **trim only** before save; check uniqueness in the service and catch MySQL duplicate-key on save.
- `Users.RoleId` FK delete behavior is **Restrict** (no cascade-delete of users when deleting a role).
- Prefer `AsNoTracking` for reads; pass `CancellationToken` to EF calls.
- Name request DTOs `userRequest` (etc.) to distinguish from entities.

## New APIs (Roles/Rights next)

- Follow Controller → `I*Service` → DbContext.
- Use `ApiResponse` / `PagedApiResponse`, permission policies, and system-role guards.
- No repository layer.
